{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1196355-discussion-on-associated-purviews-of-the-gods","id":1196355,"title":"Discussion on Associated Purviews of the Gods","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-16T21:02:57-07:00","id":1196355,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Discussion on Associated Purviews of the Gods","content":"So I noticed some peculiarities in some of the 2nd ed associated powers lists. I'm assuming/hoping for more revision before the final product. For instance wasn't Beauty one of the newer Purviews? I'm assuming because I very few gods have it, and it seems weird for Heimdall to get it but not Sif or Frejya, or friggin Aphrodite! I know he was the White God and was shiny and all but I got the impression the beauty of Sif, Freyja and Idun mythically inspired way more shenanigans then Rig's physical splendor.<br /> <br /> Also why does Loki have Epic Strength? Is it just because he is a giant? He has many stories where he is physically intimidated by blokes both giants when one in the form of an eagle threatened him into treason as it yanked him into the sky and normal sized fellas like the whole Ottars Weregild situation.<br /> <br /> And it still seems sometimes random for some beings to get the Beast Purview and others not getting it. Like if you are an Animal Headed god you probably will get it, but if you have a fondness for an animal or have some as renowned pets you only sometimes get it.<br /> <br /> And not sure I agree Njord should get the Fire Purview. From my recollection he only has that because he was stated to be able to quench any fire upon a ship, but I felt that had more to do with him being a god of the Sea rather then a master of fire. He could halt fire as a specific job related trick, he couldn't say burn a mountain to ash in a single gesture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T21:57:06-07:00","id":1196366,"title":"","content":"Neall confirmed that Aphrodite and Freyja get Beauty.<br /> <br /> You don't get Beast for having a pet. Manannan mac Lir has a horse, Poseidon invented horses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T23:23:43-07:00","id":1196380,"title":"","content":"Okay that's fair. But I mean Athena invented lots of stuff like flutes, chariots, ships ect, but she only has Supernal Weaving skills.<br /> <br /> Sometimes gods are heralded animals or symbolized by them quite strongly but they don't always get a connection with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T23:31:25-07:00","id":1196382,"title":"","content":"There's a difference between having an animal as one of your symbols, and being worshipped as the god of that animal, or you being seen as that animal incarnate.<br /> <br /> That said it is a holistic call a lot of the time, and absolutely nothing breaks if you add to or remove certain purviews to/from Gods' lists.<br /> <br /> Callings are trickier because there's the set number of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T02:12:32-07:00","id":1196419,"title":"","content":"On meditating is Loki only given Epic Strength because he causes Earthquakes when tortured?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T03:19:42-07:00","id":1196426,"title":"","content":"Earthquakes is the main reason that Poseidon gets it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T03:38:31-07:00","id":1196434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1196355-discussion-on-associated-purviews-of-the-gods?p=1196426#post1196426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Earthquakes is the main reason that Poseidon gets it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but Poseidon presumably creates Earthquakes Willingly with considerable less effort. Loki on the other hand is shown to be not significantly stronger then the average supernatural, certainly not stronger then comparable giants, and caused Earthquakes only because he was in such intense physical and emotional turmoil that he gives it his all. Its more a story about Loki being such agony rather then a story of wow Loki is so buff. I mean Loki Invented the Net and could devise cunning traps, he doesn't have Forge. Odin is very symbolically associated with Ravens due to his legendary Hunnin and Munnin, and is less tied to wolves cause of Freki and Geri because the Ravens Symbolize his mental faculties and keeping abreast of the World and was made so people would always be suspicious if anytime they see a Raven its Actually Grimnir watching them.<br /> <br /> But as seemingly proven this is still a rough draft of the powers. I'm not super upset about it. Some these I just give the sideways eye to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T10:31:47-07:00","id":1196529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1196355-discussion-on-associated-purviews-of-the-gods?p=1196419#post1196419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On meditating is Loki only given Epic Strength because he causes Earthquakes when tortured?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe Neall has commented that the reason Loki has Epic Strength is because despite being played by Tom Hiddleston in the Marvel movies, it's important to remember that Loki in the stories is <i>a full-blooded Giant</i>, who in the Eddas will wrestle Heimdall come Ragnarok.<br /> <br /> Loki isn't some delicate little waif unless they want to appear that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T18:02:04-07:00","id":1196665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1196355-discussion-on-associated-purviews-of-the-gods?p=1196529#post1196529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe Neall has commented that the reason Loki has Epic Strength is because despite being played by Tom Hiddleston in the Marvel movies, it's important to remember that Loki in the stories is <i>a full-blooded Giant</i>, who in the Eddas will wrestle Heimdall come Ragnarok.<br /> <br /> Loki isn't some delicate little waif unless they want to appear that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I Ben in the comics he was twice as strong as most asguardian males, being in the fifty ton range while most are in the 25ton range.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T17:11:15-07:00","id":1197789,"title":"","content":"So anyone know what Hel has made to be worthy of Forge?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4983-graywalker","name":"GrayWalker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T17:23:47-07:00","id":1197792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GrayWalker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1196355-discussion-on-associated-purviews-of-the-gods?p=1197789#post1197789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So anyone know what Hel has made to be worthy of Forge?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh didn't notice this. Hmm perhaps they are attributing Naglfar's construction to Hel herself? I have to meditate on this, why would she have it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T18:01:14-07:00","id":1197811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GrayWalker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1196355-discussion-on-associated-purviews-of-the-gods?p=1197789#post1197789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So anyone know what Hel has made to be worthy of Forge?</div> </div> </div> </div>I did find that odd.....<br /> <br /> Like Eldagusto, I'll have to ponder this one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T18:03:15-07:00","id":1197813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GrayWalker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1196355-discussion-on-associated-purviews-of-the-gods?p=1197789#post1197789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So anyone know what Hel has made to be worthy of Forge?</div> </div> </div> </div>That threw me too, though I do like the image of her raising her hall from the worked bone and moaning flesh of the dead. Maybe a touch of CWoD/Exalted soul-forging is at play in Helheim...<br /> <br /> (Which is her holding in the broader Realm of Nifleheim damn it! There is really no way to accurately count to 9 Realms, since just as Helheim is a location in Nifleheim, Svartalfar and Dwarves aren\u2019t actually distinguishable from each other in the myths... I lean toward just saying \u201cthe Ninth Realm is a mystery known only by Odin\u201d or possibly \u201cit\u2019s a collective label for all realms of other mythologies that exist beyond the eight actually known to the Norse.\u201d)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 03-20-2018, 09:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T18:43:22-07:00","id":1197824,"title":"","content":"I like the imagery of her knowing forge as well. She\u2019s the only god IIRC with a combo of Forge and Frost which I find to be a nice contrast.<br /> Was thinking of having my scion of Hephaestus trying to her study under her even to see a way different from his father\u2019s of forging.<br /> I just was curious about whether there was a mythic source for the domain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4983,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4983-graywalker","user":"GrayWalker","date":". 03-20-2018, 09:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4983-graywalker","name":"GrayWalker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T05:28:25-07:00","id":1206388,"title":"","content":"I'm still trying to figure out why certain purviews were made and others ditched? Biggest one is why is there a forge purview? I thought forging was something smith type gods did because that's what they did? Or that beauty is a purview now? Again just something I want to understand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23711-sessha","name":"Sessha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T07:13:44-07:00","id":1206425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sessha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1196355-discussion-on-associated-purviews-of-the-gods?p=1206388#post1206388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm still trying to figure out why certain purviews were made and others ditched? Biggest one is why is there a forge purview? I thought forging was something smith type gods did because that's what they did? Or that beauty is a purview now? Again just something I want to understand.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because there are Gods of the Forge and Gods of Beauty in myth. Beauty was included in 1E, it was just called \u201cEpic Appearance\u201d back then. The lack of a purview to allow one to play a magical Smith was a major blind spot in 1E.<br /> <br /> No Purviews from 1E were really dropped, though some were moved under Callings (Guardian being the most obvious; while the Justice Purview is divided between the Judge Calling and Order Purview).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 04-13-2018, 10:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T07:48:56-07:00","id":1206442,"title":"","content":"It should be noted: Loki's struggles that cause earthquakes are also while he is bound by the intestines of his own son, because he could break any other bonds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1778-morsrattus","name":"MorsRattus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1778_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T07:49:43-07:00","id":1206444,"title":"","content":"Also, we DID lose the Magic Purview, but that was a good thing. The parts of it that mattered survive as Fortune.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1778-morsrattus","name":"MorsRattus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1778_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T07:54:28-07:00","id":1206447,"title":"","content":"The Magic Purview was always a weird one to me as well. It was mostly revolving around working the weaves of Fate and such rather than being you know...magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23711-sessha","name":"Sessha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T07:57:01-07:00","id":1206448,"title":"","content":"'Magic' cannot be adequately defined or limited to a single Purview.<br /> <br /> Everything is magic. Nothing is magic. What counts as 'sorcery' or 'magic' for one pantheon is just the natural workings of a god in the next. Zeus can hurl thunderbolts - is that magic? When Djehuty pulls down part of the moon to make an eye for Horus, is that magic? How about when Balor unveils his eye?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1778-morsrattus","name":"MorsRattus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1778_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T08:07:48-07:00","id":1206450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sessha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1196355-discussion-on-associated-purviews-of-the-gods?p=1206447#post1206447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Magic Purview was always a weird one to me as well. It was mostly revolving around working the weaves of Fate and such rather than being you know...magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>The 1e Magic purview in Hero even mentions &quot;Okay any Scion can fling fire around and fly, sounds pretty magical.&quot;<br /> <br /> Now if it were me I would have stopped and said &quot;Do we even NEED this Purview?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T08:31:17-07:00","id":1206463,"title":"","content":"Alright here is one for you guys. Which Pantheon Specific purview did you think was one of the better ones? Personally I thought the Norse purview was one of the weakest of the lot of them. The Greeks were pretty good in the early game but their usefulness kind of tapered a bit before honestly plateauing once you got to Demigod or above.Where as the Japanese, Loa and to a lesser extent Aztecs ranged from fairly okay in the aspect of the Aztecs to pretty damn useful for the Japanese and Loa with the Egyptians being somewhere in the middle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23711-sessha","name":"Sessha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T08:46:43-07:00","id":1206474,"title":"","content":"1e: The Japanese PSP was the most fun to use (to me at least) but i felt that the greek one was the most versatile/useful.<br /> <br /> 2e: they all look very good and useful so i really cant make a distinction from best to worst until i tried them for a spin and from what i read none of them is really bad. But i can say that i'm most impatient about trying the metamorphisis purview of the greek pantheon. I know i'm gonna have a lot of fun with that one <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T08:52:21-07:00","id":1206478,"title":"","content":"I can see what you mean about the Greek being very versatile. Honestly if it came down to it pound for pound a melee Greek Scion would have a much greater chance of winning in a fight with his sword against a similar kitted out scion largely because of their Arte dice pool being used to add more dice or using dice to do re-rolls. Which I do admit is actually pretty damn boss of an ability. Though trying to max out your Arte on all your skills could get...expensive and would reach a point where you would have o ask yourself was it really worth the XP cost?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23711-sessha","name":"Sessha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T10:30:07-07:00","id":1206512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MorsRattus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1196355-discussion-on-associated-purviews-of-the-gods?p=1206442#post1206442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It should be noted: Loki's struggles that cause earthquakes are also while he is bound by the intestines of his own son, because he could break any other bonds.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'mma need citation that that was why his intestines were used, because from all my reading the intestines were used only because it was an extra slap to the face that they made one son kill another and he is bound by his family's organs. Not that they are of the most transcendental strength and nothing else could compare and Loki could shatter any bonds like Fenris.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T10:39:58-07:00","id":1206947,"title":"","content":"I can\u2019t find a direct citation here. However, on a metaphoric level, the only bond Loki cannot break or escape is that of family - hence the guts rather than normal chains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1778-morsrattus","name":"MorsRattus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1778_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T07:00:40-07:00","id":1207245,"title":"","content":"I'm still scratching my head over why Loki gets Epic Strength. I mean I know he's like a giant and all but all the stories I've ever read or heard have him, he uses his Cunning to get out of a situation. Rarely did he ever actually fight battles. That was more or less Thor's job. He was/is the Aesir's primary for lack of a better term beat stick with a giant hammer against their enemies. Case in point I remember reading a while ago about Loki getting into a bet with someone a forge god of some form or something, I think.(Which if any part of this story needs fixing please tell me. It's been over ten years since I read it so my memory might be pretty fuzzy on the matter.) that he would offer them his head. When the god came to collect Loki weaseled out of it by basically saying that since he hadn't promised his neck to the god that he couldn't take it as it was still attached to his shoulders that way. Again if I messed up any part of this story please correct me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23711-sessha","name":"Sessha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T07:20:47-07:00","id":1207254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sessha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1196355-discussion-on-associated-purviews-of-the-gods?p=1207245#post1207245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm still scratching my head over why Loki gets Epic Strength.</div> </div> </div> </div>I forget where i read this, but there is an account that earthquake (all earthquakes on earth, well midgard) are caused by Loki <i>physically</i> trying to break his bonds. You can argue that it isnt reason enough but it is a reason to give him epic strength. <br /> <br /> The next thing you need to take with a grain of salt cause i'm not even sure i'm remembering right. But i think i read that only Thor was physically stronger than Loki and it was one of the reason he always got stuck on ''getting Loki back'' duty. Again, not sure on that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T07:45:05-07:00","id":1207264,"title":"","content":"Eh flimsy at best as far as I'm concerned. As for your story and such...eh it's about on par with the one I remember about Loki so we are both in the same boat on that one.<br /> <br /> No if anything That Rock should be at least a minor god or demigod maybe in the Greeks. After all it spent how many centuries trapped in Chronos's belly? I mean that's got to count for something towards deityhood right? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Yes it's a joke. If anyone is wondering about it. I'm talking about the rock Rhea who is Zeus' mother feeding her husband Chronos a rock in place of her son. Since he'd gobbled up the rest of her children.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23711-sessha","name":"Sessha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T07:52:03-07:00","id":1207267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sessha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1196355-discussion-on-associated-purviews-of-the-gods?p=1207264#post1207264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No if anything That Rock should be at least a minor god or demigod maybe in the Greeks. After all it spent how many centuries trapped in Chronos's belly? I mean that's got to count for something towards deityhood right? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Yes it's a joke. If anyone is wondering about it. I'm talking about the rock Rhea who is Zeus' mother feeding her husband Chronos a rock in place of her son. Since he'd gobbled up the rest of her children.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well presumably That Rock would be shaped like a baby so i do think there would be inspiration for a Created type of scion there.<br /> <br /> Also, minor nitpick, i apologise but Kronos (or Cronus) is the one who ate That Rock and Zeus' siblings. Chronos is the greek god of time. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T08:03:56-07:00","id":1207275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1196355-discussion-on-associated-purviews-of-the-gods?p=1207267#post1207267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well presumably That Rock would be shaped like a baby so i do think there would be inspiration for a Created type of scion there.<br /> <br /> Also, minor nitpick, i apologise but Kronos (or Cronus) is the one who ate That Rock and Zeus' siblings. Chronos is the greek god of time. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Eee gads! Do you know what this means! It means we know the origin of the clay used to shape Wonder Woman! Shocking! Dun Dun Dun! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Ah I see. I always thought it was spelled with a &quot;C&quot; Ah well learn something new everyday I suppose. Since I know how it's spelled I'll use it in the future.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23711-sessha","name":"Sessha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T10:39:04-07:00","id":1207323,"title":"","content":"It can be spelled with a C. The only difference between Cronus the King of the Titans and Chronus God of Time is whether or not it has an h","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T11:08:42-07:00","id":1207337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1196355-discussion-on-associated-purviews-of-the-gods?p=1196380#post1196380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay that's fair. But I mean Athena invented lots of stuff like flutes, chariots, ships ect, but she only has Supernal Weaving skills.<br /> <br /> Sometimes gods are heralded animals or symbolized by them quite strongly but they don't always get a connection with them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Poseidon is attributed to being the God of Horses, in addition to being the God of the Sea and God of Earthquakes. <br /> <br /> I don't know much about Celtic mythology, but is <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Manannan mac Lir's </span></span></span> divinity associated with horses, or does he simply have one on hand?<br /> <br /> Because Thor has a pair of self resurrecting goats, and I don't recall him being the God of Goats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T11:17:04-07:00","id":1207341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1196355-discussion-on-associated-purviews-of-the-gods?p=1207323#post1207323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It can be spelled with a C. The only difference between Cronus the King of the Titans and Chronus God of Time is whether or not it has an h</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23711-sessha","name":"Sessha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T11:29:58-07:00","id":1207345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sessha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1196355-discussion-on-associated-purviews-of-the-gods?p=1206478#post1206478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see what you mean about the Greek being very versatile. Honestly if it came down to it pound for pound a melee Greek Scion would have a much greater chance of winning in a fight with his sword against a similar kitted out scion largely because of their Arte dice pool being used to add more dice or using dice to do re-rolls. Which I do admit is actually pretty damn boss of an ability. Though trying to max out your Arte on all your skills could get...expensive and would reach a point where you would have o ask yourself was it really worth the XP cost?</div> </div> </div> </div>In terms of mechanical use, Arete was probably the best bang for your buck in 1e, overall.<br /> <br /> In terms of being exciting or interesting, Arete was terrible. It was probably the dullest Purview of 1e. Even if other Purviews were markedly less useful (Jotenblut, Prophecy) but &quot;More Dice!&quot; is insomnia-curing in how dull it is.<br /> <br /> Okay, more dice or rerolls. Very useful, but still dull<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sessha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1196355-discussion-on-associated-purviews-of-the-gods?p=1207264#post1207264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh flimsy at best as far as I'm concerned. As for your story and such...eh it's about on par with the one I remember about Loki so we are both in the same boat on that one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, Loki's set to fight I think Heimdall to a standstill come Ragnarok, so the dude was <i>never</i> a wimp.<br /> <br /> Combined with &quot;Causes Earthquakes through his struggles against his bonds&quot; and &quot;Remember he's a <i>frick-fracking GIANT</i>, like full-blood Giant&quot;, it makes perfect sense to me that he has Epic Strength. I mean just because he <i>prefers</i> to use his wits and trickery doesn't mean he can't go &quot;... SCREW IT! PLAN B!&quot; and punch someone in the face.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 04-15-2018, 03:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T17:02:28-07:00","id":1207454,"title":"","content":"Chronos isn't really a god so much as just a personification of Time, really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1778-morsrattus","name":"MorsRattus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1778_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"