dited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T20:22:06-07:00","id":1207510,"title":"","content":"I thought it was Uranus that was castrated by Cronus?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/744-korusef","name":"Korusef","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar744_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"510"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T20:27:54-07:00","id":1207516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korusef</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1196355-discussion-on-associated-purviews-of-the-gods?p=1207510#post1207510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought it was Uranus that was castrated by Cronus?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but we are just rolling with the misconceptions after the Chronos isn't Cronus mention. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T01:16:18-07:00","id":1207577,"title":"","content":"It was a spelling mistake on my part that ended up being a joke, but hey I'm game to roll with it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23711-sessha","name":"Sessha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T03:15:34-07:00","id":1207598,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the double post here but I have a question about the deities for 2nd Ed. What purviews and such are being associated with Hestia? I was thinking about building her as a playable goddess in 1st since that's what I am running. Also was going to use her as the template for building Kojin since basically him and Hestia about share the same purviews basically. She goddess of fire and hearth and he is a Japanese god of FIRE, hearth and cooking. Yeah I know the Japanese having a fire deity. It's shocking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23711-sessha","name":"Sessha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T05:49:12-07:00","id":1207623,"title":"","content":"Hestia has Fire, Fortune, Order, and Prosperity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Scion 2E</b> Freelancer: <i>Origin; Hero; Demigod; God; Mythical Denizens; Mysteries of the World; Saints &amp; Monsters; No Gods, No Masters; Once &amp; Future, Realms of Magic &amp; Mystery</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/369-geoffrey","name":"Geoffrey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T06:01:24-07:00","id":1207626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geoffrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1196355-discussion-on-associated-purviews-of-the-gods?p=1207623#post1207623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hestia has Fire, Fortune, Order, and Prosperity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright going to need some explaination of Fortune and Prosperity. Which not going to lie aren't those two kind of the same thing? Just saying... but yeah also ideas on how to convert those to the purviews from 1st ed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23711-sessha","name":"Sessha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T06:12:16-07:00","id":1207628,"title":"","content":"Fortune is all about blessings, curses, chance, destiny, etc... Prosperity is all about wealth, money, and well, prosperity.<br /> <br /> Can't speak to 1e, I'm not familiar enough with it, I'm afraid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever","name":"ffanxii4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T06:18:07-07:00","id":1207631,"title":"","content":"Mmm from the sound of it she might have Prophecy, Magic or Mystery purviews. Though right now I'm kind of more leaning towards Magic more than the other two based on what you showed me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23711-sessha","name":"Sessha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T10:17:24-07:00","id":1207692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sessha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1196355-discussion-on-associated-purviews-of-the-gods?p=1207631#post1207631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mmm from the sound of it she might have Prophecy, Magic or Mystery purviews. Though right now I'm kind of more leaning towards Magic more than the other two based on what you showed me.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I remember of the Prophecy, Magic, or Mystery Purviews... Which isn't much because they were all kind of terrible...<br /> <br /> Whichever ones were about blessings and fortune. That rules out Prophecy. IIRC, Mystery is about pulling clues from nothing, so that's a maybe if at all. Perhaps with the very ill-named Magic.<br /> <br /> To say nothing of which Epic Attributes Hestia gets. The Epic Socials seem unlikely, as she herself is a very modest wallflower of a Goddess. Perhaps Epic Stamina, maybe one of the Epic Mentals?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 04-16-2018, 01:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T12:57:43-07:00","id":1207735,"title":"","content":"Hmm I think Fire, Magic and Mystery would be good then since it seems like she has a rather interesting philosophy on things. As for Epics I would with Epic Stamina, Epic Intelligence and Epic Charisma. Now why I mentioned Epic Charisma? Well I did a little digging on Hestia and I found out that worship of Hestia was quite interesting.<br /> <br /> It seemed that because she was such an instrumental and integral part of Ancient Greek culture. Namely when people would burn offerings to the gods(and it didn't matter who got it.) Hestia always got apart of all those offerings. Namely when they offered like animals or something she would always take a portion of the animal fat and keep the hearth fire burning on Mount Olympus. It was also done out of respect for her since she is the oldest the Olympians(And the oldest daughter no less) that she was that respected.<br /> <br /> Also in much of Greek culture while she seems like a wallflower she's actually not. It can be looked at as her giving up her seat &quot;among the twelve&quot; as a means of her understanding the complex social issues that come from infighting and rather than risk such a measure she gracefully offered up her seat to Dionysus. Also it wasn't considered a new colony or village until you brought a piece of the fire from a temple of Hestia to light the hearth in the new village. That's...pretty interesting to say the least. Which all that was from a cursory search about Hestia..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23711,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23711-sessha","user":"Sessha","date":". 04-16-2018, 04:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23711-sessha","name":"Sessha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T19:40:22-07:00","id":1207846,"title":"","content":"It's something to note, incidentally, that the &quot;Hestia giving up her throne to Dionysos&quot; thing isn't an actual myth. It dates back to a Robert Graves book from the mid-fifties, and while Graves was a talented storyteller (which is why this story gets repeated as much as it did), his works are not a good reference for genuine mythology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12989-center-of-all","name":"Center-of-All","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T06:43:57-07:00","id":1207964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sessha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1196355-discussion-on-associated-purviews-of-the-gods?p=1207735#post1207735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It can be looked at as her giving up her seat &quot;among the twelve&quot; as a means of her understanding the complex social issues that come from infighting and rather than risk such a measure she gracefully offered up her seat to Dionysus.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I might be seeing some 'influence' from Rick Riordan here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T06:43:57-07:00","id":1207965,"title":"","content":"..........","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12300,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","user":"Crying","date":".  Accidental double post, why can't you delete stuff on here? 04-17-2018, 09:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T07:11:25-07:00","id":1207973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crying</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1196355-discussion-on-associated-purviews-of-the-gods?p=1207964#post1207964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I might be seeing some 'influence' from Rick Riordan here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly couldn't tell you as this is the first time I have ever heard of this person myself.<br /> <br /> Now that I've done Hestia it's time to get to work on another deity. A fire deity for the Amatsukami. Yea believe it or not they do have two of them in the pantheon. Though as far as Scion is concerned one of them is a Titan...uh...okay...never saw that one but w/e. The other is a good fire deity for sure. His name is Kojin. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/K\u014djin\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/K\u014djin</a> for those who want to see a bit more before doing their own search on the interweb. He's almost as far as what he is a god of almost the exact duplicate of Hestia. Sort of. He's the God of Fire, Hearth and...Cooking of all things. Yeah that one tossed me for a bit of a loop as well.So don't feel too bad about that one.<br /> <br /> So for purviews obviously we have Fire maybe health and after reading a bit more Guardian and maybe Justice. As for epics...eh Stamina, Perception and Maybe Wits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23711,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23711-sessha","user":"Sessha","date":". 04-17-2018, 10:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23711-sessha","name":"Sessha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T08:12:49-07:00","id":1207989,"title":"","content":"That makes me wonder. <br /> <br /> In 2e what purview or calling would one associate with cooking?<br /> I mean, i'm looking at the Creator callings knacks and those could work for cooking, tho they are funny. <br /> <br /> There is:<br /> Reverse Engineer: When you take apart an object, you instantly gain an understanding of how to rebuild it, or create new versions.<br /> or<br /> Innate Toolkit: You are always able to work your craft, regardless of whether or not you have the appropriate tools available. When you use your bare hands to build or create something that would otherwise require special equipment, you suffer no penalty or any kind of Injury.<br /> <br /> And i'm just laughing imagining a scion putting his hands in a cake and going '' So this is the ingredients used''. And then making the whole cake using just his hands.<br /> <br /> I dont know if another Calling might work better tho.<br /> <br /> As for the purviews ... maybe Artistry (cooking) could work?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T13:11:40-07:00","id":1208129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1196355-discussion-on-associated-purviews-of-the-gods?p=1207989#post1207989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That makes me wonder. <br /> <br /> In 2e what purview or calling would one associate with cooking?<br /> I mean, i'm looking at the Creator callings knacks and those could work for cooking, tho they are funny. <br /> <br /> There is:<br /> Reverse Engineer: When you take apart an object, you instantly gain an understanding of how to rebuild it, or create new versions.<br /> or<br /> Innate Toolkit: You are always able to work your craft, regardless of whether or not you have the appropriate tools available. When you use your bare hands to build or create something that would otherwise require special equipment, you suffer no penalty or any kind of Injury.<br /> <br /> And i'm just laughing imagining a scion putting his hands in a cake and going '' So this is the ingredients used''. And then making the whole cake using just his hands.<br /> <br /> I dont know if another Calling might work better tho.<br /> <br /> As for the purviews ... maybe Artistry (cooking) could work?</div> </div> </div> </div>Artistry is mentioned as having 'cuisine' as a potential focus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T13:53:56-07:00","id":1208158,"title":"","content":"The Shen and Aesir are the two pantheons I know with prominent cooking gods and it will help with others too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T14:59:05-07:00","id":1208198,"title":"","content":"Kagutsuchi was most likely classed as a titan in 1E (and probably 2E) because, well... he doesn't actually do much of anything, mythologically speaking. He's born, burning his mother to death in the process, and Izanagi beheads him and cuts his body up into a bunch of other kami (which works reasonably well as a version of a &quot;bound into Tartarus&quot; myth that the structure of 1e necessitated). Plus, it's not like most mythologies have a nice, clear dividing line between god and titan anyway. The Norse mostly do, as do the Hittites, but the actual Titans from Graeco-Roman myth weren't materially different than the standard Olympians, and some (like Cronus/Saturn) were important and actively worshipped throughout the heyday of that religion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12989-center-of-all","name":"Center-of-All","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T05:41:09-07:00","id":1208817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Center-of-All</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1196355-discussion-on-associated-purviews-of-the-gods?p=1208198#post1208198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kagutsuchi was most likely classed as a titan in 1E (and probably 2E) because, well... he doesn't actually do much of anything, mythologically speaking. He's born, burning his mother to death in the process, and Izanagi beheads him and cuts his body up into a bunch of other kami (which works reasonably well as a version of a &quot;bound into Tartarus&quot; myth that the structure of 1e necessitated). Plus, it's not like most mythologies have a nice, clear dividing line between god and titan anyway. The Norse mostly do, as do the Hittites, but the actual Titans from Graeco-Roman myth weren't materially different than the standard Olympians, and some (like Cronus/Saturn) were important and actively worshipped throughout the heyday of that religion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah they pretty much pigeon holed Kagutsuchi into a titan in 1st Ed. Though in all honesty the interesting part I've found about him,(much like many of the kami) that he was also worshiped as a god of the forge. Though they did create another fire deity later called Kojin who wasn't that bad of guy. If anything from what I've been able to gather about him he as a pretty chill dude. I mean after all he was the god of cooks. I mean unless the person is a terrible cook how can you not help but like the chef am I right? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also on a different subject. I was curious since I'll be doing back conversion on him later on as well. What sort of purviews did they give Takemikazuchi?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23711-sessha","name":"Sessha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T11:26:29-07:00","id":1208955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sessha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1196355-discussion-on-associated-purviews-of-the-gods?p=1208817#post1208817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah they pretty much pigeon holed Kagutsuchi into a titan in 1st Ed. Though in all honesty the interesting part I've found about him,(much like many of the kami) that he was also worshiped as a god of the forge. Though they did create another fire deity later called Kojin who wasn't that bad of guy. If anything from what I've been able to gather about him he as a pretty chill dude. I mean after all he was the god of cooks. I mean unless the person is a terrible cook how can you not help but like the chef am I right? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also on a different subject. I was curious since I'll be doing back conversion on him later on as well. What sort of purviews did they give Takemikazuchi?</div> </div> </div> </div>Callings : Guardian, Leader, Warrior<br /> <br /> Purviews : Beasts (Deer), Epic Dexterity, Epic Stamina, Epic Strength, Sky, War","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T13:23:14-07:00","id":1208994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1196355-discussion-on-associated-purviews-of-the-gods?p=1208955#post1208955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Callings : Guardian, Leader, Warrior<br /> <br /> Purviews : Beasts (Deer), Epic Dexterity, Epic Stamina, Epic Strength, Sky, War</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah good thank you very much. Although I have to ask, How does a Stag factor into his lore as an animal? I don't think I've ever seen that associated with him. Otherwise this one is actually pretty damn easy to back convert to 1st Ed. Just add Guardian to purviews and golden.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23711-sessha","name":"Sessha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T05:20:32-07:00","id":1209191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://incidentalnaturalist.com/2015/06/24/the-sacred-deer-of-nara/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/incidentalnaturalist.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/06/dsc_0523.jpg?fit=1200%2C797&amp;ssl=1\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://incidentalnaturalist.com/2015/06/24/the-sacred-deer-of-nara/\" target=\"_blank\"> The Sacred Deer of Nara </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://incidentalnaturalist.com/2015/06/24/the-sacred-deer-of-nara/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://incidentalnaturalist.com/2015/06/24/the-sacred-deer-of-nara/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Over a thousand years ago,&nbsp;the great Shinto deity,&nbsp;Takemikazuchi-no-mikoto rode into the Japanese city of Nara on the back of a white deer.&nbsp;In the year 768, Takemikazuchi-no-mikoto was enshrined wi&hellip; </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1778-morsrattus","name":"MorsRattus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1778_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T05:22:12-07:00","id":1209192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sessha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1196355-discussion-on-associated-purviews-of-the-gods?p=1208994#post1208994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah good thank you very much. Although I have to ask, How does a Stag factor into his lore as an animal? I don't think I've ever seen that associated with him. Otherwise this one is actually pretty damn easy to back convert to 1st Ed. Just add Guardian to purviews and golden.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tame deer run all over the place in his shrines at both Kasuga and Kashima. That is because a deer was the creature sent to fetch Takemikazuchi when the Amatsukami had need of him, and was the creature he rode from Kashima to Kasuga on when he wanted to found that new shrine. Thus deer also feature heavily in his sacral art.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T05:44:47-07:00","id":1209202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sacerdos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1196355-discussion-on-associated-purviews-of-the-gods?p=1209192#post1209192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tame deer run all over the place in his shrines at both Kasuga and Kashima. That is because a deer was the creature sent to fetch Takemikazuchi when the Amatsukami had need of him, and was the creature he rode from Kashima to Kasuga on when he wanted to found that new shrine. Thus deer also feature heavily in his sacral art.</div> </div> </div> </div>So then I once more stand corrected. Guess they did more of their homework this time around. Which if I had ever tried to play 2nd Ed.(which will be never) Take would be my go to man as he's pretty much covers what I want in a deity for a warrior.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23711-sessha","name":"Sessha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T11:47:43-07:00","id":1209339,"title":"","content":"I mean Odin doesn\u2019t get Ravens and they are usually depicted in the art...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}